{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions","id":500300,"title":"2e Seeming Predictions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-02T07:26:31-07:00","id":500300,"title":"2e Seeming Predictions","content":"So this thread probably won't be relevant for terribly long, but it popped up in the Darkling thread and I thought it would be best to have a topic specifically for this. Now that we have two examples of 2e Seemings, we can start to establish potential patterns and use them to try to predict what direction the other four might go. So what do you think? What might the pre-durance backgrounds for the remaining Seemings look like? How did they change themselves to escape? What will their Breaking Points be? How will they regain Clarity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:52:53-07:00","id":500346,"title":"","content":"So I'd like to share my thoughts on what the Fairest might look like. So far with Beasts and Darklings, we've gotten quite a but of background on what characters of each Seeming were like before their Durance. Some people have expressed concerns that these backgrounds make the concepts too specific, but personally I disagree. I don't see it as all that different from 1e specifying why Changelings of each Seeming were usually taken, and I see the background filling a very similar purpose in 2e - to establish what kind of person is likely to end up as this Seeming. In my reading, the backgrounds are also tied in strongly with the abuse metaphor, showing how these characters were vulnerable, what it was about them that the Gentry were able to take advantage of, and what about themselves they had to change in order to escape that cycle of abuse.<br /> <br /> The pattern so far seems to be that the vulnerability is very much the opposite of the creature they had to become. So Beasts were formerly restricted, making them easy prey for their abusers to entrap, and the only way they could escape that was by becoming wild and untamable. The Wyrd took that figurative wildness and turning them into literal beasts. Darklings were formerly loyal, trusting, making them easy prey for their abusers to neglect or betray, and the only way they could escape that was by making themselves colder, darker, more pragmatic. The Wyrd took that figurative darkness and turned them into literal creatures of the dark. So, in that light, how can we apply this pattern to other Seemings?<br /> <br /> This is what lead to my prediction on the Fairest. The Fairest have always been about beauty - in 1e it was often the reason they were taken, but in the 2e paradigm where Seeming is a matter of personal agency, I would assume they had to make themselves beautiful to escape. Again, this was probably not literal, but became so due to the Wyrd. Since the backgrounds so far have been fairlt opposite of what the character became, my prediction is that the Fairest background will be people who had issues of low self-esteem and negative self-image. This ties in very well with the abuse metaphor, as people with low self-esteem are some of the most commonly victimized by abusers. This poor self-image could be what made the character vulnerable to being ovjectified in Arcadia, and their means of escape would be through developing self-worth. They escape by making themselves beautiful <i>to themselves</i>, and the Wyrd in turn makes them beautiful to everyone else.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Other predictions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:48:09-07:00","id":500452,"title":"","content":"<b>Elementals: </b>Abandon the Self and embrace the World - Clarity through rejection of of the Self - People who felt bound by themselves and let go<br /> The Zen counterpart to Beasts. Beasts break free, Elementals let go.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres:</b> Abandon discipline - Clarity through consumption/indulgence - Ascetics who had to indulge themselves<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> You were never strong enough, fix that - Clarity through ???Craft??? - Strong people who had to accept their imperfections??<br /> <br /> I have a pretty solid idea of where I think/hope they're going to go with Elementals, but the others are a bit more murky. As far as Fairest go, I'm expecting something involving either co-dependency or narcissism. From what we've seen so far it seems like Seemings will be able to map pretty well with emotional issues that can arise from PTSD. Beasts act out, Darklings can't trust, Elementals are emotionally severed, Ogres &quot;consume&quot; which can translate to substance abuse or binging, Wizened look like they'll have a bit of a thing about modifying themselves or things around them so basically people who bury themselves in their work or something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:25:24-07:00","id":500486,"title":"","content":"Interesting. The PTSD lens is definitely a cool take on the Seemings that I hadn't considered. It definitely seems to be expressed through the Blessing and Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:13:54-07:00","id":500527,"title":"","content":"I predict that Elementals leave something physical of themselves behind - like an animal gnawing off a leg to escape a trap, and heal the wound using something primordial","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:05:47-07:00","id":500590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions?p=500452#post500452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Elementals: </b>Abandon the Self and embrace the World - Clarity through rejection of of the Self - People who felt bound by themselves and let go<br /> The Zen counterpart to Beasts. Beasts break free, Elementals let go.<br /> <br /> <b>Ogres:</b> Abandon discipline - Clarity through consumption/indulgence - Ascetics who had to indulge themselves<br /> <br /> <b>Wizened:</b> You were never strong enough, fix that - Clarity through ???Craft??? - Strong people who had to accept their imperfections??<br /> <br /> I have a pretty solid idea of where I think/hope they're going to go with Elementals, but the others are a bit more murky. As far as Fairest go, I'm expecting something involving either co-dependency or narcissism. From what we've seen so far it seems like Seemings will be able to map pretty well with emotional issues that can arise from PTSD. Beasts act out, Darklings can't trust, Elementals are emotionally severed, Ogres &quot;consume&quot; which can translate to substance abuse or binging, Wizened look like they'll have a bit of a thing about modifying themselves or things around them so basically people who bury themselves in their work or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hunch that Elementals and Wizened are going to be mirror-images of each other, with Wizened being people who were drifting, aimless, looking for a purpose, and found a way out through finding something important to them, while Elementals were dependent/obsessive types who escaped by learning how to let go, how to give something up.<br /> <br /> Ogres, I think, are going to be about self-denial, the sort who are very harsh on themselves, denying themselves pleasure in pursuit of a goal. Workaholics, say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T13:35:54-07:00","id":500739,"title":"","content":"I would think that <b>Ogres</b> escaped by violence: storm the exit from Arcadia, beat up the guards, set an ambush for the Huntsmen when they track you down in the Hedge (they won't make that same mistake twice, though...). I predict that they gain Clarity when they solve a problem with violence, and suffer a breaking point when they face a threat they can't fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T14:22:13-07:00","id":500776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions?p=500739#post500739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that <b>Ogres</b> escaped by violence: storm the exit from Arcadia, beat up the guards, set an ambush for the Huntsmen when they track you down in the Hedge (they won't make that same mistake twice, though...). I predict that they gain Clarity when they solve a problem with violence, and suffer a breaking point when they face a threat they can't fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what I was thinking as well. I figure the background would be someone who was unassertive prior to their Durance, being taken because they were unable to fight back at the time, and they changed themselves by becoming stronger, more able to fight their way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:21:24-07:00","id":500842,"title":"","content":"I believe one of the Devs said Ogres would have something to do with Consumption. Not sure what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T16:18:58-07:00","id":500893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions?p=500842#post500842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe one of the Devs said Ogres would have something to do with Consumption. Not sure what.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do remember Dave saying something along these lines, now that you mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:31:57-07:00","id":501109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions?p=500842#post500842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe one of the Devs said Ogres would have something to do with Consumption. Not sure what.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, before their Durances, Ogres could be people with great appetites (read: Vices in general). Maybe they took their consumption for granted, or maybe they were stingy about it. The Gentry take these people by tempting them with feasts calculated for their appetites. The victims take Agency and become Ogres by somehow learning that life isn't all about consumption. Their escapes were filled with traps that consisted not of spike pits or falling cages, but tables of food, shiny treasures and the like. In addition to that, Ogres learn that they really &quot;Are What They Eat&quot;: they regain Clarity by indulging their appetites after hard and just work, but lose it if they get it into trouble for accepting a quick fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:06:40-07:00","id":501201,"title":"","content":"Well, Fairest preview is out, I was way off! I like it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:46:33-07:00","id":563380,"title":"","content":"So, just had a thought. Maybe Wizened are the ones who earned their way out of Arcadia, beating sone sort of riddle or test or otherwise besting the obstacles set against them with skill and determination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:57:37-07:00","id":563776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/500300-2e-seeming-predictions?p=563380#post563380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just had a thought. Maybe Wizened are the ones who earned their way out of Arcadia, beating sone sort of riddle or test or otherwise besting the obstacles set against them with skill and determination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as they are fea-tools hybrids in Kiths preview, I would rather assume you &quot;overworked&quot; yourself to escape. Like Santa Claws elves prepering tools to run away when making toys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}